NAME
       shmget, shmat, shmdt, shmctl - shared memory

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/shm.h>

       int   shmget(key_t key, size_t size, int flag);
       void *shmat(int id, const void *addr, int flag);
       int   shmdt(const void *addr);
       int   shmctl(int id, int cmd, struct shmid_ds *buf);

DESCRIPTION
       System V shared memory. shmget creates or looks up a segment by
       key, shmat maps it into the address space, shmdt unmaps it, and
       shmctl with IPC_RMID marks it for removal.

       A segment stays alive while any process has it attached, and the
       kernel detaches whatever a process still holds when it exits.

RETURN VALUE
       An id or an address on success, -1 with errno set. shmat returns
       (void *)-1 on failure.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   no such segment and IPC_CREAT was not given
       ENOMEM   not enough memory
       EINVAL   bad id or size

SEE ALSO
       semget(2), mmap(2), shmtest(1)
